        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "Live RSA in both copies of the tutorial's PKI layer: OpenSSL::PKey::RSA.new(2048) keygen (stage3:5, stage6:6), private_encrypt (stage3:11/stage6:12), public_decrypt (stage3:16/stage6:17) — a textbook RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SIGNATURE scheme used to sign blockchain transactions (PKI.sign is called from Transaction#initialize, stage6/block.rb:76). The collector's variant RSA-ENC/pke with an ML-KEM (key-transport) remediation misreads the call: the completing ops are private_encrypt/public_decrypt, i.e. si"
